"""Omarchy Music: a minimal YouTube Music popup, themed live from Omarchy.

YouTube Music is the library: your playlists, likes, search and radio. The
audio comes from Tidal in FLAC: each song is matched there by title, artist
and length, downloaded once (the first time it plays, or by the background
sync of all your playlists) and played from disk after that. Songs Tidal has
no lossless copy of are skipped. The next song in the queue is fetched ahead
so tracks change without a gap.

  omarchy-music                open, or toggle the popup if it is already running
  omarchy-music --tidal-login  connect Tidal from a terminal (the Library tab can too)
  Files: ~/Music/YouTube Music/  (songs/, art/, library.json, missing.json)

Media keys work through MPRIS (playerctl); mpv does the playback.
"""
